title: empty strings from kanban-md are still read as values in five more places
updated: 2026-08-10T03:55:11Z
---

Follow-up to #59, which fixed the pickability predicate, list rendering and
context overdue. The root cause -- an attribute that is set to the empty string
counts as having a value -- is still live elsewhere. Each verified, not inferred:

- Cmd/Board.pm:179,204  counts claims against literal done/archived, and treats
                        claimed_by: "" as claimed
- Cmd/Show.pm:78        prints "Claimed:  " with nothing after it
- Role/TaskMutation.pm:161  reads claimed_by: "" as a live claim
- Foundation.pm:523     same

The clean fix is one line rather than five, and was deliberately left out of #59
because it changes the bytes written for every imported card and two lanes were
running in those files at the time. In App::karr::Task::BUILD, replacing the
!defined test:

    next unless $self->$has;
    my $v = $self->$attr;
    $self->$clearer if !defined $v || !length $v;   # 0 and "0" keep length 1

That matches Go`s omitempty, which is where the asymmetry comes from in the
first place. It needs a deliberate decision because it is a storage change:
a card imported from kanban-md then written back by karr loses the empty keys.
That is almost certainly right -- kanban-md re-adds them on its own writes -- but
it should be someone`s decision, with a round-trip test.

Related and NOT covered by the one-liner: Task::update_timestamps stamps
completed only on a move into a literal "done", so on a board whose terminal
status is "shipped" no completion is ever recorded. Verified. Fixing it changes
the method signature, which Move, Edit, Archive, Handoff and TaskMutation all
call.
